---
/**
 * Two animated sessions doing the same job, with a running token counter.
 *
 * READ THIS BEFORE TRUSTING THE ANIMATION
 *
 * The text that scrolls is RECONSTRUCTED. What a model actually emits is not
 * reproducible on demand, so these are realistic sessions of the shape the two
 * architectures produce — not recordings. Calling this a "live replay" would be a lie
 * of the most expensive kind, because it would borrow the authority of a trace.
 *
 * What IS measured is every token figure the counters reach: real tools/list from a
 * live @modelcontextprotocol/server-filesystem session, real tool results, real `f`
 * output from the built binary, tokenized with o200k_base.
 * scripts/measure-streams.mjs regenerates them and cross-checks read_text_file at 260
 * against the figure published in /docs/measurements/.
 *
 * THE FAIRNESS DECISION, STATED IN THE UI
 *
 * f needs a shell tool; no model runs `f` without one. So this is not "schema vs no
 * schema" — both sides carry a tool definition. The real difference is whose
 * capabilities are declared: MCP declares fourteen filesystem tools, f declares one
 * generic runner and relies on knowledge it supplies through the index. The shell
 * definition is paid by both sides and is therefore subtracted from the difference;
 * it is 44 tokens, shown rather than hidden, because a difference that survives
 * subtraction is the difference.
 *
 * The animation is the point, not decoration: MCP's cost is that its definition block
 * is present on every turn, which is invisible in a static screenshot and obvious when
 * the counter climbs 2,877 before the model has said anything.
 */

// From scripts/measure-streams.mjs.
const MCP = {
  tools: 14,
  defs: 2877,
  calls: [29, 26],
  results: [46, 236],
};
const F = {
  shellDef: 44, // paid by both sides
  index: 57,
  calls: [15, 13],
  results: [42, 15],
};

// Per-turn cumulative totals the counters animate to. Everything both sides pay (the
// shell definition) is included on both, so the two columns are directly comparable.
const mcpTurns = [
  { n: "1", what: "definitions registered", tok: MCP.defs, cum: MCP.defs },
  { n: "2", what: "read_text_file → contents", tok: MCP.calls[0] + MCP.results[0], cum: MCP.defs * 2 + MCP.calls[0] + MCP.results[0] },
  { n: "3", what: "directory_tree → listing", tok: MCP.calls[1] + MCP.results[1], cum: MCP.defs * 3 + MCP.calls[0] + MCP.results[0] + MCP.calls[1] + MCP.results[1] },
];
const fTurns = [
  { n: "1", what: "bash def + `f` → index", tok: F.shellDef + F.index, cum: F.shellDef + F.index },
  { n: "2", what: "f creds get prod.db", tok: F.calls[0] + F.results[0], cum: F.shellDef + F.index + F.calls[0] + F.results[0] },
  { n: "3", what: "f creds status", tok: F.calls[1] + F.results[1], cum: F.shellDef + F.index + F.calls[0] + F.results[0] + F.calls[1] + F.results[1] },
];
const total = (t) => t.at(-1).cum;
const shellNote = `${F.shellDef} tokens of bash definition are paid by both sides and counted on both`;
---

<div class="compare">
  <p class="compare-job">
    The same three-turn job, both ways. Counters are measured payloads; the text is a
    realistic reconstruction, not a recording. {shellNote}.
  </p>

  <div class="compare-panes">
    <section class="compare-col" aria-label="Simulated session using MCP tools">
      <p class="compare-head">
        <span class="compare-svc">MCP</span>
        <span class="compare-sub">{MCP.tools} tools declared</span>
        <span class="compare-count" data-count-for="mcp" data-count-to={total(mcpTurns)}><b>0</b> tokens</span>
      </p>
      <div class="stream" data-stream="mcp">
        <div class="turn">
          <p class="turn-h">turn 1 <span>{mcpTurns[0].cum}</span></p>
          <pre class="ln body">system: you are an agent with these tools…
tools: read_text_file, write_file, edit_file,
       create_directory, list_directory, directory_tree,
       move_file, search_files, get_file_info, …
       <em>14 definitions, every request</em></pre>
        </div>
        <div class="turn">
          <p class="turn-h">turn 2 <span>{mcpTurns[1].cum}</span></p>
          <pre class="ln asst">{`{ "type": "tool_use", "name": "read_text_file",
  "input": { "path": "/tmp/mcpsim/notes/creds.md" } }`}</pre>
          <pre class="ln tool">{`{ "content": [ { "type": "text",
  "text": "prod.db\n  host: db.internal\n  user: svc\n" } ] }`}</pre>
        </div>
        <div class="turn">
          <p class="turn-h">turn 3 <span>{mcpTurns[2].cum}</span></p>
          <pre class="ln asst">{`{ "type": "tool_use", "name": "directory_tree",
  "input": { "path": "/tmp/mcpsim", "excludePatterns": [] } }`}</pre>
          <pre class="ln tool">{`{ "content": [ { "type": "text", "text": "[
 { "name": "notes", "type": "directory",
   "children": [ { "name": "creds.md",
     "type": "file" } ] } ]" } ] }`}</pre>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="compare-col" aria-label="Simulated session using f">
      <p class="compare-head">
        <span class="compare-svc f">f</span>
        <span class="compare-sub">1 tool declared</span>
        <span class="compare-count" data-count-for="f" data-count-to={total(fTurns)}><b>0</b> tokens</span>
      </p>
      <div class="stream" data-stream="f">
        <div class="turn">
          <p class="turn-h">turn 1 <span>{fTurns[0].cum}</span></p>
          <pre class="ln body">system: you are an agent with these tools…
tools: bash
$ f
f v0.3.3
config creds df fj gh ha providers search uck</pre>
        </div>
        <div class="turn">
          <p class="turn-h">turn 2 <span>{fTurns[1].cum}</span></p>
          <pre class="ln asst">{`{ "tool": "bash",
  "input": { "command": "f creds get prod.db" } }`}</pre>
          <pre class="ln tool">prod.db = sk-live-9f2c… (expires in 2h 14m)</pre>
        </div>
        <div class="turn">
          <p class="turn-h">turn 3 <span>{fTurns[2].cum}</span></p>
          <pre class="ln asst">{`{ "tool": "bash",
  "input": { "command": "f creds status" } }`}</pre>
          <pre class="ln tool">unlocked (167m 31s left)</pre>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>

  <p class="compare-verdict">
    <b>{total(mcpTurns).toLocaleString()}</b> against <b>{total(fTurns)}</b> for three
    turns. The gap is not the calls — those are {MCP.calls[0]} and {F.calls[0]} tokens —
    it is {MCP.defs.toLocaleString()} of definitions riding on every turn. 
    <a href="/docs/measurements/">how these were measured</a>
  </p>
</div>
